---
.title = "VS Code",
.description = "The same watchers beside VS Code, in its status bar and output channel.",
.date = .date("2026-10-21T00:00:02"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
---


The same test watchers run beside VS Code as beside Neovim, from the same `watchers.json` and `.overwatch.json`: the full suite first, then the watcher, with no agent involved. zanity does not run here either; its own `zanity lsp` gives the editor its findings. The latest result of each language's watcher is in the status bar, which turns red while any build fails. Every failing build goes into the overwatch output channel, titled with its watcher and cleared of each one as it goes green; clicking the status bar, or Show report on the notification, opens it. A watcher with no `argv` reruns `baseline` after every save, stopping a run that a newer save has overtaken. A watcher that exits is restarted as it is in Neovim, at once or after 30 and then 60 seconds; after three quick exits in a row it stays stopped, with what it last printed, until `Overwatch: Start`. It starts with VS Code in the first workspace folder when that has a watcher; `Overwatch: Start`, `Overwatch: Stop`, `Overwatch: Show Report` and `Overwatch: Doctor` are in the command palette. It needs VS Code 1.100 or later.

With overwatch's Claude Code plugin installed as well, Claude follows VS Code's watchers instead of running its own, so a suite runs once for both. The extension watches the git repository holding the workspace folder, as Claude Code does, and writes each watcher's reports to `~/.cache/overwatch/feeds`. A Claude Code session in that repository reads them there as it would its own watcher's: failures it caused wake or join its turns, and its edits ask the extension to rerun a watcher that has no watch command. The status bar shows `→ Claude` beside each watcher a running Claude Code session follows. Claude checks at each turn: a session started before VS Code switches to VS Code's watchers, and one whose VS Code has closed goes back to running its own. A watcher the extension does not run, such as zanity, Claude still runs itself.

`Overwatch: Doctor` checks all of this: the repository being watched, each watcher and whether its tool is on PATH, whether the Claude Code plugin is installed, enabled and the same version as the extension, and whether Claude is following each watcher, naming the fix for anything that is not.
